  "details": "While using RDNA3 (7900 XTX in my case) on Windows 10:\n\n- Open VRChat via SteamVR\n\n- Focus another program like your browser, etc.\n\n- Observe frametimes while swapping focus between that program and VRChat\n\nThis seems potentially related to https://forum.unity.com/threads/game-performance-degrading-when-window-does-not-have-focus.643279/\n\nExample frametimes of two scenarios while focused and unfocused are attached. One being a synthetic \"light\" load in an avatar museum map and the other being a real \"heavy\" load in the Great Pug.\n\nIn extreme cases, it can really mess with CPU frametimes as the GPU begins producing a consistent late-start scenario for the SteamVR compositor.\n\nSince Easy Anti-Cheat is active, it is impossible to adjust priorities of the game or adjust affinities via task manager or process lasso to see if this would fix the issue.",
